    "original_title": "Somaliland oo shaacisay natiijada imtixaanaadka shahaadiga ee fasallada 12-aad iyo 8-aad",
    "slug": "somaliland-releases-grade-8-and-grade-12-exam-results-with-high-pass-rates",
    "summary": "Somaliland announced results for Grade 12 and Grade 8 exams. Pass rates were exceptionally high for both levels, with slight variations between the two.",
    "content": "Somaliland's education authorities released official results for the national certificate examinations for Grade 12 secondary students and Grade 8 middle school students on 25 August 2026. The announcement was made in Hargeisa, the administrative capital of Somaliland.\n\nFor the secondary school leaving exam, 16,078 students sat for the test. Of these, 16,051 passed, representing a success rate of 99.8%. Only 27 students, or 0.2% of the total, did not pass and will need to resit the exam. The Grade 8 exam involved a larger cohort. A total of 25,954 students participated, and 25,860 candidates passed, which equals a 99.6% pass rate. The number of students who did not pass was 94, accounting for 0.4% of the candidates.\n\nThe results demonstrate a very high level of performance among students who took the certificate exams this year. Education officials have not yet provided a detailed analysis of the results or the reasons behind the few failures, but the overall numbers point to a strong showing across both grade levels.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these results are significant as they provide a snapshot of educational attainment in Somaliland, a region that many families look to for their children's schooling. High pass rates can ease concerns about the quality and reliability of the education system for those considering sending their children back home for studies. They also serve as a basis for scholarship opportunities and further academic progression, both within the region and abroad.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/25/somaliland-oo-shaacisay-natiijada-imtixaanaadka-shahaadiga-ee-fasallada-12-aad-iyo-8-aad/",
